From: steamed-noodle <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tfa9872: fix uninitialized DC-DC config and TFA9874 DCVOS register

Two bugs in tfa987x_setup_dcdc(), the function that programs the boost
(DC-DC) converter feeding the speaker amplifiers:

1. "u32 mcc, dcvof, dcvos, dctrip, dctrip2 = 0;" only initializes dctrip2.
   The OnePlus 8 device tree sets none of the optional DC-DC properties, so
   of_property_read_u32() never writes the other four and they keep whatever
   was on the stack. op8_defconfig sets CONFIG_INIT_STACK_NONE=y, so the
   compiler does not zero them either. Depending on that garbage, the amp
   boost converter is either left disabled or programmed with arbitrary
   max coil current (DCMCC), boost voltage (DCVOF/DCVOS) and trip levels.
   Initialize all five to 0, which means "keep the chip defaults".

2. For TFA9874 (rev 0x73/0x74) the second boost voltage level DCVOS lives in
   register 0x76 (DCDC_CTRL6) bits 14:9. NXP's own field map in the OnePlus
   SM8250 vendor kernel says TFA9874_BF_DCVOS = 0x7695 (register 0x76,
   bit 9, 6 bits wide). The driver wrote it to 0x70 (DCDC_CTRL0) instead,
   where bits 14:9 hold DCDIS (DC-DC on/off, bit 14) and DCIE (adaptive
   boost, bit 9). Write it to DCDC_CTRL6. With fix 1 and no device tree
   value this path is never taken, but it must not be wrong if someone
   adds "second-boost-voltage" later.

Reference for the field map: LineageOS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8250,
techpack/audio/asoc/codecs/tfa98xx-v6/tfa9874_tfafieldnames.h
(TFA9874_BF_DCMCC = 0x7033, TFA9874_BF_DCIE = 0x7090,
TFA9874_BF_DCDIS = 0x70e0, TFA9874_BF_DCTRIP = 0x7444,
TFA9874_BF_DCTRIP2 = 0x7534, TFA9874_BF_DCVOF = 0x7635,
TFA9874_BF_DCVOS = 0x7695; encoding 0xRRPL = register, bit position,
width minus one). DCMCC, DCIE, DCTRIP, DCTRIP2 and DCVOF were checked and
already match the driver.

This does NOT add speaker protection. The driver still runs both TFA9874
amps without NXP's protection algorithm and with current/voltage sense
disabled, so long loud playback can still overheat the speakers. See
docs/hardware-safety.md in the steamed-noodle repo.

NOTE: upstream tfa9872.c uses CRLF line endings, so the hunk lines below
end in CRLF. Do not let git or an editor convert this file (see the
repo's .gitattributes).

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c	2026-10-01 16:16:29.041020676 +0300
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c	2026-10-01 16:16:29.060787580 +0300
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@
 
 static bool tfa987x_setup_dcdc(struct device *dev, struct regmap *rmap, u16 rev)
 {
-	u32 mcc, dcvof, dcvos, dctrip, dctrip2 = 0;
+	u32 mcc = 0, dcvof = 0, dcvos = 0, dctrip = 0, dctrip2 = 0;
 	int i;
 	u32 *dest[] = { &mcc, &dcvof, &dcvos, &dctrip, &dctrip2 };
 	const char *props[] = { "max-coil-current",
@@ -191,7 +191,7 @@
 					FIELD_PREP(TFA9874_DCDC_CTRL6_DCVOF_MSK, dcvof));
 
 		if (dcvos)
-			regmap_update_bits(rmap, TFA987X_DCDC_CTRL0,
+			regmap_update_bits(rmap, TFA987X_DCDC_CTRL6,
 					TFA9874_DCDC_CTRL6_DCVOS_MSK,
 					FIELD_PREP(TFA9874_DCDC_CTRL6_DCVOS_MSK, dcvos));
 		break;
